# .gitignore for the r/OneOrangeBraincell project
#
# Rule of thumb: code, the cat kit, docs, and only the data files that a script or the
# visualization actually reads. Everything else (scratch outputs, backups, review pages,
# early exploratory pulls, local tooling) stays on this machine.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- local tooling and system files
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.remember/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
~$*
*.tmp
*.part
# Stray PNGs in the top folder only (Blender review images); keeps docs/ and SVG/ images
/*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- unrelated / personal
/discussion4_full.csv
/_to_delete/
/2x/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- media cache (558 MB of Reddit users' photos and videos)
# The D3 page's "example post" pictures read from here; with it excluded, a fresh clone shows the
# cats and tails but no example photos. The media also belongs to the original posters.
# To publish it anyway, delete the next line (individual videos run up to 36 MB).
/oobc_media/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- superseded data and process outputs (root)
# Early exploratory pulls (last 30 days, last 6 months), not used by anything now
/oobc_top_30days*
/oobc_6mo_*
# Old coding sheet from the first coding scheme
/Orange Braincell Data - Sheet2.csv
# Convenience merges and review pages (rebuild with oobc_archive/join_meta.py, build_post_meta.py, oobc_cat_traits.py)
*_with_meta.csv
/oobc_heyday_2022-04_08_top40_enriched.csv
*_cats_review.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- oobc_archive process files
/oobc_archive/backups/
/oobc_archive/final_codes/codes_transcribed.txt
/oobc_archive/ai_opinion/tokenprobs/probe_test.py
/oobc_archive/bread_rerun/wqtzrl_cats_raw.jsonl
/oobc_archive/bread_rerun/wqtzrl_original_thinking.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- cat kit: exported PNGs (the SVGs are the source)
/SVG/2x/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- prototype: earlier card layout
/viz/viz_template_v1.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Blender pounce animation (kept local for now)
/blender/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Firebase Hosting (built by viz_d3/build_site.py)
/site/
/.firebase/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- exploratory analysis: per-post table (rebuilt by build_table.py; holds Reddit usernames)
/oobc_archive/exploratory/posts.csv
